# Efficiency Guidelines

## File Reading Strategy
- **Never re-explore the project structure** — see [project-architecture.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/project-architecture.mdc) for file map
- **Never `ls` data directories** — see [datasets-and-checkpoints.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/datasets-and-checkpoints.mdc) for all paths, sizes, labels
- **For paper citations**, check [paper-references.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/paper-references.mdc) before searching the full plan
- **For metric key names**, check [metric-naming.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/metric-naming.mdc)

## Large File Handling
- `code/evaluation_runner.py` is ~5900 lines. **Do NOT read the whole file.** Use semantic search or grep to find the specific `_eval_*` method or section you need.
- When the file grows past ~2000 lines per logical section, split into:
  - `code/eval_plots.py` — all `_plot_*` helper methods
  - `code/eval_metrics.py` — pure metric computation functions
  - `code/eval_utils.py` — data loading, splitting, component ID extraction

